  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Holistic Approaches and Practices in early childhood care and education (SHAPE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To elevate early childhood care and education (ECCE) globally, UNESCO is set to launch the &quot;Strengthening Holistic Approaches and Practices in Early Childhood Care and Education&quot; (SHAPE) project. This elevation is rooted in the Jomtien Declaration&apos;s assertion that &quot;education begins at birth&quot; and is further supported by the Tashkent Declaration and Commitments to Action for Transforming Early Childhood Care and Education. SHAPE aims to make ECCE a priority of education policies worldwide. It has three strategic objectives: i) elevating ECCE in-policy debates ii) enhancing accountability through data and monitoring and iii) advocating for its legal recognition.</narrative>
  </description>
